            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0386" n="262" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg262"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">707.1190h/–: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-25T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 25,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>24. Your 46, August 21, 8 a.m.</p>
                <p>Your course approved. Mission announcing accession of Amir received July 20th by
                    Secretary and 26th by President, who accepted and answered respectively letters
                    from Foreign Minister<anchor n="3" xml:id="d217-f1"/> and Amir. Overture toward
                    establishment of diplomatic relations met by pointing out necessity of
                    Congressional action and further consideration. Formal recognition of
                    independence neither asked for nor granted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
